<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mēcōnĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηκώνιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Poppy-juice</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20,
				18, 76, § 202</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 12, 91, §
			142</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant, called also</i> peplis, <i><span class="en">Plin. 27,
				12, 93, § 119</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The excrements of new-born children</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 4,
				13, § 52</span></i>.</div>
